Z||000000||DXR_DAD||10-31-1999||10:26 AM||||Wanted:  All tips on interior & upholstery repair. Type of glue used on padding? Type of paint? How to remove parts? etc.<P>PS. DaRkLoRD, This may be a good one for your web site?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Eric||10-31-1999||11:14 AM||||I basically finished restoring/customizing my interior a few weeks ago.  I installed a new headliner, painted all the light grey plastic parts of the interior black with Plastikote paint, and I'm waiting on black carpet to arrive.  There were a few odds and ends I added just to make everything look and function better.  I recovered the front speaker covers with black mesh I got from Radio Shack. I fixed all the parts where the plastic and foam material was pulling away from the frame, like the armrest, center consuls and center dash, with Krazy glue.  I put a shortened shifter in with a new carbon fiber look shift knob.  I put a full carbon fiber dash kit on (I paid about $100 too much).  I also installed pedal covers to help heal-toe downshifting.  They also look cool.  I hope to add leather seats in the future and maybe racing harnesses or atleast black webbing for the seat belts.<P>The most difficult part of the whole process was removing the dash to paint it.  It took a few hours to get everything apart.  Painting it only took a few minutes.  I taped off the upper dark gray section so there wouldn't be any reflection in the windsheild from the glossy black paint I used.<P>I'm really proud of the way my interior looks now.  I think too many people think the Fiero's insides are a lost cause, but I think nothing could be further from the truth.  Besides, doing a little customization is a lot cheaper than spending a grand on a new dash from Pisa or someplace.||||reg||1
Z||000002||four50four||10-31-1999||11:26 AM||||sounds great Eric. got any pics??||||reg||6
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||10-31-1999||12:41 PM||||Yeah, stuff like that is exactly what I'm looking for!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Dash modifications are my favorite interior Fiero mod, as I've never really liked the Fiero interior.. it's efficient, but not quite what I like. Anyone who has done modifications to the Fiero dash or other interior stuff, if you'd like to send them to me (don't forget lots of pictures!) I'll gladly put them on my website, like  <BR>DXR_DAD suggested.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>btw, I'd love to see some pics of that dash too Eric!||||reg||1
